      "heading": "The prosecution’s challenge",
      "id": "P006",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The prosecution argued that Acosta remained the accountable and bonded officer, while Lachica was neither accountable nor bonded. It said the Joint Circular did not allow the handoff, the internal paper did not expressly acknowledge receipt of the cash, and the available records did not establish who ultimately received the money or how it was used. In the prosecution’s view, reliance on one person’s account and documents was a failure of internal control."
    },
