      "heading": "The defense theory",
      "id": "P007",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The defense drew a different line between financial custody and field operations. It argued that the Joint Circular did not require a special disbursing officer to conduct confidential operations, possess operational training, or hold a security clearance. The defense further argued that Acosta could rely on a security officer designated by the head of agency. It emphasized that she examined the acknowledgement receipts, tallied the amounts, checked their stated purposes, coordinated with Lachica, and was satisfied from the submitted documents that the funds related to confidential activities."
    },
