      "heading": "What senator-judges tested",
      "id": "P008",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The senator-judges tested that defense from several angles. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan asked how Acosta could safeguard money without knowing the operations, and whether Lachica was truly the final recipient contemplated by the Joint Circular. Erwin Tulfo and Raffy Tulfo pressed the lack of a fidelity bond, the aliases, and repeated signatures. Gatchalian asked how Acosta could assure the public that the cash had not been pocketed, and why liquidation reports preceded complete acknowledgement receipts."
    },
