      "heading": "Where the session stopped",
      "id": "P009",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Escudero excused Acosta after the final questions. The court expected Limuel Ortoño, an assistant chief of staff at the Office of the Vice President, as the prosecution’s next witness, ordered Senate medical verification before deciding whether to excuse Edward D. Fajarda, and issued subpoenas for three Armed Forces of the Philippines witnesses. After the defense objected to the short notice, Escudero said the defense would receive time to prepare before cross-examination. A ruling on a separate August 12 manifestation was deferred to the following day."
